{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtTriangularCore","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GramNondegenerate","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RankMinor","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.SesquilinearForm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearForm.Orthogonal","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Group"],"declarations":42,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_isSimple_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_isSimple_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":1298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1298-L1323","doc":"**Irreducibility of `S^μ` over an ordered field — fully `sorry`-free.**\n\nThe same reduction as `specht_isSimple`, but routed through\n`specht_form_nondegenerate_ordered` (Stage 1) instead of the `CharZero` core,\nso it carries **no** `sorry` at all: `specht_submodule_dichotomy` is sorry-free\nand needs only `Field k`, and Stage 1 supplies the non-degeneracy outright.\n\nThis covers `ℚ` and `ℝ` — the archimedean evaluation the framework actually\nuses.  It also needs no `μ.card ≠ 0` hypothesis.\n\n`specht_isSimple` is the broader statement (every characteristic-zero field,\n`ℂ` included) and is **also** sorry-free now, so this variant is kept for its\ncheapness and its independence from the Cauchy–Binet chain, not because the\ngeneral case is still owed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_isSimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_isSimple","kind":"theorem","line":1275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1275-L1296","doc":"**Irreducibility of `S^μ` over any characteristic-zero field — proved.**\n\nReduces to the two cores above, both of which are now sorry-free:\n`specht_submodule_dichotomy` (James's submodule theorem) and\n`specht_form_nondegenerate` (§4.4).  `#print axioms` reports\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n\nReproduces the brick-2 statement `QOU.BraidKnot.Specht.specht_isSimple`\nverbatim; that one is still a stub, because brick 2 cannot import this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_submodule_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_submodule_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":1226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1226-L1271","doc":"**James's submodule theorem (the dichotomy)** — now proved **sorry-free modulo\nthe single core `kap_of_mem_line`**.  For any `S_n`-stable `k`-submodule `U ≤ M^μ`,\neither `S^μ ≤ U` or `U ≤ (S^μ)ᗮ`.\n\n**Proof.**  Split on whether `κ_s` annihilates all of `U`.\n* If `κ_s x = 0` for every `x ∈ U`, `s`: then for each `x ∈ U`,\n  `⟨e_s, x⟩ = ⟨κ_s {s}, x⟩ = ⟨{s}, κ_s x⟩ = 0` (`kapL_selfadjoint`), so `x ⊥ S^μ`,\n  i.e. `U ≤ (S^μ)ᗮ`.\n* Otherwise some `κ_s x ≠ 0` with `x ∈ U`.  Then `κ_s x ∈ U` (`kapL_mem_U`) and\n  `κ_s x ∈ span{e_s}` (`kapL_mem_line`), so `κ_s x = c·e_s` with `c ≠ 0`, whence\n  `e_s ∈ U`.  By `S_n`-equivariance (`polytabloid_rep_equivariant`) and\n  transitivity (`tableau_transitive`) every polytabloid lies in `U`, so\n  `S^μ ≤ U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.spechtPerp_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.spechtPerp_stable","kind":"theorem","line":1199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1199-L1222","doc":"`(S^μ)ᗮ` is `S_n`-stable — the form is invariant, so the complement supplied\nby `isCompl_specht_perp` is a complement **of representations**, not merely of\n`k`-modules.  This is the half that makes the extension in Sagan §2.4.4 a\nhomomorphism of `k[S_n]`-modules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.isCompl_specht_perp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.isCompl_specht_perp","kind":"theorem","line":1178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1178-L1197","doc":"**`M^μ = S^μ ⊕ (S^μ)ᗮ`.** The Specht module and its form-orthogonal\ncomplement are complementary submodules of `M^μ`.\n\nMathlib supplies the implication\n(`LinearMap.BilinForm.isCompl_orthogonal_of_restrict_nondegenerate`); what was\nmissing until §4.4 was its hypothesis, non-degeneracy of the form restricted to\n`S^μ`, which over a general characteristic-zero field is exactly\n`specht_form_nondegenerate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_form_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_form_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":1028,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1028-L1167","doc":"**Non-degeneracy of the form on `S^μ`, every characteristic-zero field** —\n`S^μ ⊓ (S^μ)ᗮ = ⊥`.  Formerly this module's last `sorry`; now proved.\n\n**Historical warning, kept because the wrong route is tempting.**  An earlier\nplan read\n\n> `0 = ⟨e_T, x⟩ = Σ_S c_S ⟨e_T, e_S⟩ = c_T · |C_T|`, off-diagonal entries\n> being `0`\n\nwhich presumes the standard-polytabloid Gram matrix is diagonal.  It is not —\nsee the refutation block above: `μ = (2,1)` gives `[[2,1],[1,2]]`.  Do not\nrestate `specht_gram_orthogonal`.\n\n**The proof, in five moves.**\n\n*1. Thin the polytabloids over `ℚ`.*  `exists_linearIndepOn_extension` picks a\nsub**set of tableaux** `b` whose polytabloids are `ℚ`-independent and still\ncover the rest.  It is stated for `LinearIndepOn` over a `Set ι`, so what comes\nback is a set of *tableaux*, not of vectors — which is why this step needs no\nstandard-basis theorem, no Garnir straightening, and no dominance core.\n\n*2. Their coordinate matrix is an integer matrix.*  A polytabloid is a signed\nsum of basis tabloids, so every coefficient is a sum of `±1`\n(`SpechtBaseChange.polytabloid_apply_eq_intCast`).  Call it `Mz`.\n\n*3. `det (Mz Mzᵀ) ≠ 0` over `k`.*  `RankMinor.exists_selector_det_ne_zero` turns\nthe `ℚ`-independence of `Mz`'s rows into a nonzero maximal minor, and\n`CauchyBinet.det_gram_map_ne_zero` turns that into the Gram determinant being\nnonzero in `k`.  **This is the step that reaches `ℂ`**: Cauchy–Binet writes\n`det (Mz Mzᵀ) = Σ_f (det Mz_f)²`, a sum of squares *of integers*, so the\npositivity argument happens entirely in `ℤ` and `k` is never ordered.\n\n*4. That determinant is the Gram determinant of the form.*  The tabloid basis is\northonormal for `bilinM` (`bilinM_apply`), so the Gram matrix of any family is\nexactly `(coordinate matrix) · (coordinate matrix)ᵀ`.\n\n*5. Invertible Gram ⇒ trivial radical.*\n`GramNondegenerate.span_inf_orthogonalBilin_eq_bot`.\n\nThe family spans over `k` and not merely over `ℚ` because the coordinates are\nintegers, so the `ℚ`-relations found in step 1 survive base change\n(`SpechtBaseChange.spechtSubmodule_eq_span_of_rat`).\n\n**Relation to Stage 1.**  `specht_form_nondegenerate_ordered` (§4.3-bis) proves\nthe same statement over an ordered field by positive definiteness, in three\nlines.  It remains as the cheap special case; it provably cannot reach `ℂ`,\nwhere the form is bilinear rather than sesquilinear and has isotropic vectors\n(`x = (1, i)` gives `⟨x, x⟩ = 0` with `x ≠ 0`).\n\n**No `μ.card ≠ 0` hypothesis.**  Earlier versions carried one, to match the\nbrick-2 contract in `Specht.specht_isSimple`.  That stub has since been deleted\n(it duplicated a proved theorem), and the proof never used the hypothesis, so it\nis gone: the statement holds for the empty diagram too.  Dropping it matters\ndownstream — `isCompl_specht_perp` below could not be stated for every `μ` while\nits input demanded a nonemptiness proof that `μ = ∅` cannot supply.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_not_le_perp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_not_le_perp","kind":"theorem","line":1005,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L1005-L1026","doc":"**In characteristic zero the form does not vanish on `S^μ`.**  Immediate\nfrom `bilinM_polytabloid_self`: `⟨e_t, e_t⟩ = |C_t|`, and `|C_t| ≥ 1` is a\npositive natural number, hence nonzero in a `CharZero` field.\n\nThis rules out the `S^μ ≤ R` branch when `specht_submodule_dichotomy` is\napplied to the radical `R = S^μ ⊓ (S^μ)ᗮ`.  As the section note above explains,\nthe surviving branch is vacuous, so this is *not* a route to\n`specht_form_nondegenerate` — it is the honest statement of how much the\ndiagonal Gram entry buys on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_polytabloid_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_polytabloid_self","kind":"theorem","line":931,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L931-L1003","doc":"**Diagonal Gram entry:** `⟨e_t, e_t⟩ = |C_t|`, the order of the column\nstabilizer — for *any* tableau `t`; standardness is not used.\n\nThe `|C_t|` tabloids `{π • t}` for `π ∈ C_t` are pairwise distinct, because\n`{π • t} = {σ • t}` forces `σ⁻¹π ∈ R_t ⊓ C_t = {1}`\n(`SpechtTriangularCore.colStab_inf_rowStab_eq_one`).  So the double sum\ncollapses onto its diagonal, where each term contributes `sgn(π)^2 = 1`.\n\n**Provenance.**  Proved sorry-free in commit `2815c29a1` as a `private` lemma\nabout *standard* polytabloids, then removed when the neighbouring\n`specht_gram_orthogonal` was refuted — the module docstring's \"recover from git\nhistory\" note refers to exactly this.  The refutation concerned the\n*off-diagonal* entries only; this diagonal computation was always correct.  It\nis restored here for a general tableau, since the proof never used\nstandardness, and made public because both stages of the non-degeneracy plan\nconsume it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_form_nondegenerate_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.specht_form_nondegenerate_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":886,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L886-L902","doc":"**Stage 1 of the corrected plan for `specht_form_nondegenerate`.**  Over an\nordered field the form is positive definite on *all* of `M^μ`\n(`bilinM_self_eq_zero_iff`), so `S^μ ⊓ (S^μ)ᗮ = ⊥` is immediate: an element of\nthe intersection is orthogonal to itself, hence zero.\n\nNote this needs **no** `μ.card ≠ 0` hypothesis and no standard-basis or Gram\ninput, so on the fields it covers it is strictly stronger than the `CharZero`\nstatement below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_self_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_self_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L866-L884","doc":"**The form is positive definite over an ordered field.**  In the tabloid\nbasis `⟨x, x⟩ = Σ_d (x d)^2` is a sum of squares, so it vanishes exactly at\n`x = 0`.  No Specht theory enters — this is a statement about `M^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_mem_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_mem_line","kind":"theorem","line":735,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L735-L751","doc":"`κ_t` lands in the polytabloid line for **every** input — sorry-free from the\ncore `kap_of_mem_line`, by `Finsupp` linearity over the tabloid basis\n(`κ_t (Σ c_d {d}) = Σ c_d · κ_t {d}`, each `κ_t {d} ∈ span{e_t}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line","kind":"theorem","line":694,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L694-L733","doc":"**Core 1 — the column-clash lemma (`κ_t` lands in the polytabloid line).**\nFor any tableaux `t, s`, the column-antisymmetrised basis vector\n`κ_t {s} = Σ_{π ∈ C_t} sgn(π) {π•s}` is a scalar multiple of the polytabloid\n`e_t`, i.e. it lies in `span_k {e_t}`.  This is the irreducible combinatorial\nheart of James's submodule theorem ([james1984representation] §8; [sagan2001]\n§2.4, the \"sign-reversing involution\" lemma).  **Two cases:**\n\n* *Column clash* (`kap_of_mem_line_clash`, **sorry-free**) — if two labels lie in a\n  common column of `t` and a common row of `s`, the transposition of those labels\n  is a sign-reversing involution of the `C_t`-sum fixing every tabloid `{π•s}`, so\n  `κ_t {s} = 0 ∈ span{e_t}`.\n* *No clash* (`kap_of_mem_line_match`, **sorry-free**, applied to `π₀` from\n  `noclash_match_exists`) — the labels in each column of `t` occupy distinct\n  `s`-rows, so some `π₀ ∈ C_t` row-matches `s` to `t` (`{π₀•s} = {t}`), giving\n  `κ_t {s} = sgn(π₀)·e_t`.\n\nThis lemma is thus **fully proved sorry-free**: both legs are discharged, and the\nmatching existence `noclash_match_exists` they consume is now proved (§4.x) from\nelementary `YoungDiagram` counting.  Everything downstream — `kapL_mem_line`, and\nhence `specht_submodule_dichotomy` (§4.5) — is therefore sorry-free, closing the\nformer opaque `specht_submodule_dichotomy` stub entirely (mirroring how\n`SpechtDominanceCore` reduced brick 4's dominance content, but here with the residual\ncombinatorial obligation also carried out). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.noclash_match_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.noclash_match_exists","kind":"theorem","line":631,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L631-L692","doc":"**Core 1′ — the residual pure-combinatorial matching (no module theory).**\nIf no column of `t` shares two labels with a common row of `s` (the *no-clash*\nhypothesis), then some column permutation `π₀ ∈ C_t` carries the tabloid `{s}`\nonto `{t}`.  This is the Gale–Ryser / conjugate-partition matching fact\n([sagan2001] §2.4, Lemma 2.4.4; [james1984representation] §8): the labels of each\ncolumn of `t` occupy, under `s`, exactly the rows `{0, …, h_c − 1}` — the unique\n`0/1` matrix with the conjugate-partition margins is the Young diagram itself.\nIt was the sole remaining combinatorial obligation of `kap_of_mem_line`; it is now\ndischarged (§4.x) from the elementary `YoungDiagram` counting helpers, so — with the\nclash leg and the reindexing leg both already `sorry`-free — `kap_of_mem_line` is\nfully closed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.Col_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.Col_card","kind":"theorem","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L536-L543","doc":"The labels in column `c` of a tableau `t` number `colLen c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.colCells_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.colCells_card","kind":"theorem","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L519-L534","doc":"Cells of `μ` in column `c` and rows `< r` number `min r (colLen c)` (columns are\ndownward-closed initial segments of rows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.filterCard_reindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.filterCard_reindex","kind":"theorem","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L503-L517","doc":"Reindex a label-filter cardinality through a tableau bijection to the corresponding\ncell-filter on `μ.cells`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line_match","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L460-L490","doc":"**No-clash matching leg (sorry-free).**  If some `π₀ ∈ C_t` carries the\ntabloid `{s}` onto `{t}` (`{π₀ • s} = {t}`), then `κ_t {s} = sgn(π₀) · e_t`, hence\nlies in `span {e_t}`.  Proved by reindexing the `C_t`-sum through right\nmultiplication by `π₀` (a bijection of `C_t`) and using that `{ρ • (π₀ • s)} =\n{ρ • t}` for every `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line_clash","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kap_of_mem_line_clash","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L390-L458","doc":"**Clash leg of the column-clash lemma (sorry-free).**  If two *distinct*\nlabels `a ≠ b` lie in a common column of `t` (`colPattern t a = colPattern t b`)\nand a common row of `s` (`rowPattern s a = rowPattern s b`), then `κ_t {s} = 0`:\nthe transposition `τ = (a b)` is a sign-reversing involution of the `C_t`-sum\nfixing every tabloid `{π • s}`, so the sum cancels in pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.mtab_of_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.mtab_of_congr","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L383-L388","doc":"`Mtab.of` depends only on the tabloid class: row-equivalent tableaux give the\nsame basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.tableau_transitive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.tableau_transitive","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L365-L372","doc":"The `S_n`-action on tableaux is **transitive** (both are bijections\n`Fin n ≃ μ.cells`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.polytabloid_rep_equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.polytabloid_rep_equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L342-L363","doc":"**`S_n`-equivariance of polytabloids**: `rep σ e_s = e_{σ•s}`.  Reindex the\n`C_s` sum by `conjEquiv`; signs match by `sign_conj`, tabloids by the\n`C_{σ•s}`-cell identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.sign_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.sign_conj","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L335-L340","doc":"Conjugation preserves the sign of a permutation (in the commutative unit\ngroup `ℤˣ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.conjEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.conjEquiv","kind":"def","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L316-L333","doc":"The **conjugation bijection** `C_s ≃ C_{σ•s}`, `π ↦ σ π σ⁻¹`.  Column\nstabilizers of `S_n`-translates are conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_selfadjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_selfadjoint","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L304-L314","doc":"**`κ_t` is self-adjoint** for the form: `⟨κ_t x, y⟩ = ⟨x, κ_t y⟩`.\n`sgn` is inversion-invariant and the form is `S_n`-invariant, so reindexing the\ncolumn sum by `π ↦ π⁻¹` swaps the operator across the pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_rep_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_rep_swap","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L298-L302","doc":"`⟨rep σ x, y⟩ = ⟨x, rep σ⁻¹ y⟩`, from `S_n`-invariance of the form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_zsmul_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_zsmul_right","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L294-L296","doc":"`⟨a, c • b⟩ = c • ⟨a, b⟩` (integer scalar). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_zsmul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_zsmul_left","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L289-L292","doc":"`⟨c • a, b⟩ = c • ⟨a, b⟩` (integer scalar). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.rep_mul_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.rep_mul_apply","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L285-L287","doc":"Multiplicativity of the representation on application. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_mem_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_mem_U","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L277-L283","doc":"`κ_t` preserves any `S_n`-stable submodule (it is a `ℤ`-combination of the\ngroup action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_of_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_of_self","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L273-L275","doc":"`κ_t {t} = e_t`: the polytabloid is `κ_t` of its own basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_of","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L266-L271","doc":"`κ_t` on a basis tableau vector is the signed column sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL_apply","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L258-L264","doc":"Pointwise value of `κ_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.kapL","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L251-L256","doc":"The **column antisymmetrizer** `κ_t : M^μ →ₗ M^μ`,\n`κ_t = Σ_{π ∈ C_t} sgn(π) · rep(π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.mem_spechtPerp_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.mem_spechtPerp_iff","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L225-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.spechtPerp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.spechtPerp","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L221-L223","doc":"The form-orthogonal complement `(S^μ)ᗮ` of the Specht module inside `M^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_rep_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_rep_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L194-L217","doc":"**`S_n`-invariance.** The representation `Mtab.rep` preserves the form:\n`⟨rep σ f, rep σ g⟩ = ⟨f, g⟩`.  (The action permutes the orthonormal tabloid\nbasis.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L187-L190","doc":"`IsSymm` packaging of `bilinM_symm` (so the orthogonal complement is\nreflexive — needed to commute orthogonality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_symm","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L181-L185","doc":"The form is **symmetric**: `⟨f, g⟩ = ⟨g, f⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_eq_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_eq_flip","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L170-L179","doc":"The form equals its flip — the bilinear-map form of symmetry.  Proved by\nreducing to basis pairs via `Finsupp.lhom_ext` and `mul_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_single_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_single_single","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L159-L168","doc":"**Basis orthonormality.** `⟨⟦d⟧, ⟦e⟧⟩ = δ_{d,e}`: the tabloid basis is\northonormal for the form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM_apply","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L149-L157","doc":"Evaluation of the form: `⟨f, g⟩ = Σ_{d ∈ supp f} f d · g d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible.bilinM","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtIrreducible.lean#L140-L147","doc":"The **standard symmetric bilinear form** on `M^μ` for which the tabloid basis\nis orthonormal: `⟨f, g⟩ = Σ_d (f d) · (g d)`.  Built `sorry`-free as\n`Finsupp.lsum`, hence bilinear by construction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}